1
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:23,891
<v OLIVIA>Hi Zach! I heard you passed your driving test! Congratulations!


2
00:02:23,891 --> 00:02:27,409
<v ZACH>Thanks Olivia! I passed just last week. 

3
00:02:27,409 --> 00:02:31,448
<v ZACH>It feels great to be independent and driving on my own!


4
00:02:31,448 --> 00:02:42,645
<v OLIVIA>I really want to take driving lessons, but I haven’t been able to find a driving school that will give lessons during the weekends . So I have to miss any classes at college. 


5
00:02:42,645 --> 00:02:50,557
<v ZACH>The driving school that I used was brilliant and really flexible with their teaching hours. It’s really close to school. 


6
00:02:50,557 --> 00:02:59,300
<v ZACH>It’s really close to school. The address is 67 King’s Road - that’s 67-KING-apostrophe-S Road.


7
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:04,233
<v OLIVIA>Oh that’s perfect! I don’t like the idea of driving around busy streets.

8
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:11,099
<v OLIVIA>Did your teacher make you drive in urban areas or did he mainly teach you on roads in the countryside?


9
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:18,156
<v ZACH>My teacher said that I had to learn on both in order to become a good and experienced driver.

10
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:22,977
<v ZACH>We would start in the city centre and then drive north above the city.

11
00:03:22,977 --> 00:03:25,361
<v OLIVIA>He sounds like a good teacher. 

12
00:03:25,361 --> 00:03:29,621
<v OLIVIA>Would you mind giving me his contact details so I can ask him for lessons?


13
00:03:29,621 --> 00:03:37,292
<v ZACH>Of course! My mother’s friend Daniel Smith referred me to him. His name is Allen Sutcliffe.


14
00:03:37,292 --> 00:03:39,420
<v OLIVIA>Could you spell the surname please? 


15
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:45,721
<v ZACH> S-U-T-C-L-I-double F-E.

16
00:03:45,721 --> 00:03:49,551
<v OLIVIA>Thanks for helping me out, I’ll give him a call tomorrow.

17
00:03:49,551 --> 00:03:53,671
<v OLIVIA>I don’t know if I should learn in a manual or automatic car. 

18
00:03:53,671 --> 00:03:54,997
<v OLIVIA>How do I decide?


19
00:03:54,997 --> 00:03:59,137
<v ZACH>I wasn’t sure which type of car to learn in either.

20
00:03:59,137 --> 00:04:08,096
<v ZACH>In the end I chose to learn in a manual car because once you’ve learnt how to drive manually you can drive automatic as well. 

21
00:04:08,096 --> 00:04:11,772
<v ZACH>Most cars on the road are automatic nowadays.


22
00:04:11,772 --> 00:04:11,872
<v OLIVIA>OK, I think I’ll learn with a manual car too then. 

23
00:04:15,987 --> 00:04:20,827
<v OLIVIA>Hopefully the teacher will be able to give me lessons in the evenings after school!


24
00:04:20,827 --> 00:04:24,955
<v ZACH>It would be much better if you take the lessons during the day.

25
00:04:24,955 --> 00:04:32,824
 <v ZACH>It will be far easier for you to learn when there is enough daylight to clearly see everything going on around you.

26
00:04:32,824 --> 00:04:38,360
<v ZACH>But you need to be an experienced driver to drive safely at night.


27
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:47,183
<v OLIVIA>How frustrating! I was hoping I wouldn’t have to take lessons during the weekends! You’re right though, safety comes first!


28
00:05:22,252 --> 00:05:26,580
<v ZACH>Speaking of safety, you should wait until summer to start learning! 

29
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:36,765
<v ZACH>It’s really difficult and dangerous to drive in the wind and rain as a learner so you should definitely wait until the weather is sunny and dry.


30
00:05:36,765 --> 00:05:39,596
<v OLIVIA>OK, that’s perfect, actually!

31
00:05:39,596 --> 00:05:43,639
<v OLIVIA>It will give me some time to save up some money to pay for the lessons.


32
00:05:43,639 --> 00:05:49,502
<v ZACH>Tell me about it! I had to work for months before I had enough money saved up!

33
00:05:49,502 --> 00:05:54,395
<v ZACH>It was worth all the work when I finally got my driving license though!


34
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:59,481
<v OLIVIA>The whole process is so expensive! How much did it cost you in the end?


35
00:05:59,481 --> 00:06:10,681
<v ZACH>Well, each half hour lesson cost $30 and then the final test cost $50. In total it cost me about $300.


36
00:06:10,681 --> 00:06:17,090
<v OLIVIA>Gosh, it’s pretty expensive! How did you find the test? Was it really difficult?


37
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:22,434
<v ZACH>No, it wasn’t too bad, and the man was really calm and friendly.

38
00:06:22,434 --> 00:06:31,198
<v ZACH>I knew that I would have to perform two parking manoeuvres during the test, so I practised them a lot beforehand and that really helped!

39
00:06:31,198 --> 00:06:36,194
<v ZACH>The test used to last 40 minutes, but it changed a bit.

40
00:06:36,194 --> 00:06:50,470
<v ZACH>For the first 20 minutes of the test he gave me directions and I had to just drive around and then the last 10 minutes was for demonstrating the manoeuvres, so the test is 30 minutes in total.	

41
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:55,585
<v OLIVIA>OK, great, I’ll remember that! Do you have any more advice?


42
00:06:55,585 --> 00:07:01,163
<v ZACH>It’s really good to practise driving a lot outside of driving lessons as well. 

43
00:07:01,163 --> 00:07:06,567
<v ZACH>Whenever my parents were running errands on the weekends I would offer to drive them. 

44
00:07:06,567 --> 00:07:13,935
<v ZACH>My driving teacher also told me to buy a notebook to write down everything that I’ve learnt in it like a  diary.


45
00:07:13,935 --> 00:07:18,889
<v OLIVIA>Haha, that sounds boring, but I’ll do it if it helps.


46
00:07:18,889 --> 00:07:28,853
<v ZACH>I found it really useful! Before my test I read through everything I had written down and it reminded me of a lot of things that I had forgotten about!

47
00:07:28,853 --> 00:07:35,569
 <v ZACH>It’s really helpful for the theory test as well because there’s so much information to remember for it.


48
00:07:35,569 --> 00:07:38,780
<v OLIVIA>That’s great, Zach! Thanks for your help! 


49
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,764
<v ZACH>No problem, see you at school!


50
00:07:40,764 --> 00:07:42,009
<v OLIVIA>Bye!